 * never considers `device_worker_id` — and then `reconcilePin` pins that row to
 * the sole fresh device with a bare UPDATE. When the org holds a SECOND live row
 * that already carries the fresh device, the UPDATE violates the index, aborts
 * the surrounding transaction, and the wire attempt fails on every poll.
 *
 * Observed on prod 2026-07-29: org 8dc12bdd held apple.computer_use rows 397
 * (device 2c295bed…) and 447 (device e7806c72…), emitting 21 identical
 * "[device-connectors] Failed to wire device connector /
 * duplicate key value violates unique constraint" errors in 10 minutes.
 *
 * These tests drive the exported entry point, NOT a hand-copied UPDATE — the
 * bug lives in production SQL and must be reproduced through it.
